==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[gwailo]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|yue|en}} {{term|鬼佬||tr=gweilo|lang=yue|foreign devil}}, from {{term|||lang=yue|ghost}} + {{term|佬||lang=yue|a regular guy, a chap}} {{rfscript|Chinese|also proper transcriptions}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{derogatory}} A [[w:Caucasian race|Caucasian]] person (generally a man).

====Usage notes====
For the usage in Cantonese, see the usage notes at [[鬼佬]].

Some Caucasians living in [[w:Hong Kong|Hong Kong]] now occasionally use the English '''gweilo''' to jokingly refer to themselves.

In the Hong Kong cinema industry, '''gweilo''' is often used to describe Caucasian actors playing in Asian movies.

